// ===========================================================================
// nightshade/tools/spellfx_shot.hml — LOOK AT THE SPELLS          (spell-fx)
// ===========================================================================
//
//   hemlockc -O1 tools/spellfx_shot.hml -o /tmp/spellfx
//   DISPLAY=:0 /tmp/spellfx --sheet /tmp/spells.png
//   DISPLAY=:0 /tmp/spellfx --scene heal --tod 22 --out /tmp/heal_night.png
//   DISPLAY=:0 /tmp/spellfx --list
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.  CLAUDE.md rule 8: "LOOK at every frame you change — a
// number saying 'fixed' while the picture is wrong is not fixed."  The spell FX
// have no call site in the shipping game yet (`main.hml` is not this task's file
// and does not know the school exists), so without this harness the only thing
// anybody could look at is the 16x16 atlas cells — and the whole brief is about
// what they look like AT 320x240 IN A SCENE, at night and in daylight.
//
// ⚠ RENDER WITH DISPLAY=:0.  Under `SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy` SDL picks the
// SOFTWARE renderer, which collapses BLEND_ADD to BLEND inside
// SDL_RenderGeometry — every additive FX pixel in this project is meaningless
// under it.  `fxgen.hml` says the same thing about its own measurements.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT THIS HARNESS IS AND IS NOT
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// IS: the real frame graph (`src/render/world_render.hml`), the real art
// (palette, tod, texgen, skygen, fxgen, meshgen), the real additive atlas
// through the real `fx_emit`, the real ToD at a real hour, and the real spell
// FX layer driven at a real 1/60 s timestep.  Every pixel of the effects comes
// from `src/art/fxgen.hml` and `src/render/fx.hml` and nothing here fakes any
// of it.
//
// IS NOT: `tools/shot.hml`.  That file is the project's primary visual
// instrument and owns the scene registry, the eight critic scenes, the props,
// the structures, the HUD and the stats contract.  This is a much smaller
// thing — grass, a hill, a lantern-lit night, and one spell going off — and it
// exists because this task may not edit `shot.hml`.  When the spell FX get a
// call site in `main.hml`, the right home for these scenes is `shot.hml`'s
// registry and this file should be deleted.
//
// DETERMINISTIC: no wall clock reaches any decision.  The camera, the terrain
// seed and the spell timeline are all fixed, `tod_reset()` runs before every
// evaluation, and `fx_spell_update` is stepped with a literal dt.  The same
// command produces byte-identical PNG bytes; `--selftest` proves it.
// ===========================================================================

